        <span class="badge-favourite">Favourite</span>
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Writing Instruments</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Pilot Custom 74 Fountain Pen</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">The pen I reach for every day, without exception. The fine nib is precisely calibrated; the balance in the hand is near perfect. Japanese engineering at its most considered.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£95 — £120</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-card" data-category="stationery">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item2/500/400" alt="Notebook">
        <span class="badge-new">New Find</span>
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Notebooks</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Leuchtturm1917 A5 Dotted</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">I have tried many notebooks. This is the one I always return to. The paper takes ink beautifully without feathering; the dot grid is unobtrusive enough to forget it's there.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£18 — £22</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-card" data-category="stationery">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item3/500/400" alt="Ink">
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Ink</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Diamine Oxblood Fountain Pen Ink</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">A deep burgundy-brown with wonderful character — it reads as dark in dim light and reveals its redness in sunlight. Ideal for correspondence that should look as though it was written with intention.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£8</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-card" data-category="stationery">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item4/500/400" alt="Pencil">
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Pencils</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Blackwing 602 Pencils</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">The pencil of Steinbeck and Nabokov and a great many other writers who cared about such things. The semi-firm lead is perfect for prose drafts; the eraser is unmatched. A luxury with a case.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£22 for 12</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="section-divider"><span>Books &amp; Editions</span></div>

  <div class="items-grid">

    <div class="item-card" data-category="books">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item5/500/400" alt="Folio Society">
        <span class="badge-favourite">Favourite</span>
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Fine Editions</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Folio Society Selected Editions</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">I buy Folio editions selectively, for books I expect to read more than once. The physical quality — paper, binding, illustration — is consistently superb. Their Middlemarch and Collected Poems of Keats are particularly fine.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£30 — £100+</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-card" data-category="books">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item6/500/400" alt="Art book">
        <span class="badge-new">New</span>
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Art Books</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">The Art of the Book: Illuminated Manuscripts</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">Published by Thames & Hudson, this survey of medieval manuscript illumination is itself a beautiful object — large format, excellent colour reproduction, and scholarship that never loses sight of the images.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£55</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="item-card" data-category="books">
      <div class="item-image">
        <img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/item7/500/400" alt="Poetry">
      </div>
      <div class="item-body">
        <p class="item-category">Poetry</p>
        <h3 class="item-name">Faber Poetry Classics Series</h3>
        <p class="item-desc">The Faber clothbound poets — Larkin, Hughes, Plath, Heaney — are beautifully produced at a sensible price. These are books you can carry without anxiety and lend without regret.</p>
        <p class="item-price">£14 — £18</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

